                <pb facs="0627" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3711a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-11T18:00:00-04:00">June 11, 1940—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>164. From the Under Secretary. A broadcast this afternoon announced that
                    “President Vargas of Brazil in a public speech has alluded to the European
                    dictatorships in a complimentary manner”. Please telegraph immediately any basis
                    there may be for this report. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
